Published Decompression, Oxygen Toxicity, and Gas Physics Models Implemented:
- Dr. Albert A. Bühlmann ZH-L16C (Compartment 1b and Compartment 1) dissolved-gas
  decompression model
- Haldane (isobaric) and Schreiner (linear depth-change) inert gas transport
  equations
- Erik C. Baker Gradient Factors (GF Low / GF High) ceiling and linear ramp model
- NOAA / Erik C. Baker 7-segment piecewise linear CNS % oxygen toxicity model
  and 90-minute half-time surface interval decay
- Lambertsen / Baker Pulmonary Oxygen Toxicity Units (OTU / UPTD) model
- Real-Gas Virial Z-factor compressibility equations and UHMS/DAN gas density
  reference thresholds (5.2 g/L and 6.2 g/L)

